# spec_id: eravos.organism.particle-field · version 1.0.0 · phase P54 · status canonical (generated from code, then owned by the spec)
identity:
  id: eravos.particle-field ; label: Field ; icon: ✺ ; accent: "#7cf7ff" ; category: Visuals
  comp_intent: A particle field that moves with the music — bass pulls it in, hits burst it out — and remembers the song’s key as basins.
  engine_notes: |
    Listens through a tap (never reroutes). Each analyser frame becomes forces: bass → gravity in, onsets → bursts out,
    mids → curl, highs → entropy, chroma → 12 basins on a circle of fifths. The basins are the memory: notes heard
    dig them, unheard ones fill back in with a half-life of Memory seconds; the memory is saved with the project.
    Physics after the CFR kernel (curl noise, attractors, stress events, soft walls), rewritten seeded and DOM-free
    as window.EravosField. UI draws WebGL2 points (2D canvas fallback).
tests: standard_tests + particle-field.test.js

